  <ym-title|Actual all-matched palette warning:
  evidence><label|actual-all-matched-palette-warning-evidence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Canonical task: issue #26, unit YM-000026.

    <item>Status: author draft; independent mathematical/source review
    pending.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-palette-warning.tex>.

    <item>Source pin: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Scope: finite weighted-response arithmetic, the same-selected-pilot
    local zero-socket argument, and the source quantifier join that yields
    the two palette clauses. The global kernel/source/move prices are
    supplied by the parent unit <verbatim|sec:actual-global-row-prices>; this
    unit does not claim to derive them.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  content>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified source
  declarations>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned source
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|Active-to-row response
  map, source, mean, direct row, and auxiliary
  row>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.SectorChange.Rows.move>, <verbatim|source>,
  <verbatim|blame>, <verbatim|direct>, <verbatim|eta>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.SectorChange.meanLog>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/SectorNext/GAUSSIAN_SECTOR_CHANGE/{Affine,Remainder,Chosen}.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|move>
  has response-row coordinates (slots and color) as its rows and active
  link-color coordinates as its columns. Thus the source transport is
  <verbatim|move\<#1D40\> source>, the selected mean is minus the transpose
  of the panelized Gram matrix times that transport, and the direct response
  is <verbatim|move*mean + source>. The auxiliary row is
  <verbatim|-g\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>(gram*mean + blame)>; the displayed
  defect form is algebraically equivalent.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform global
  kernel, gap, and window-defect prices>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.MarginalMultiplier3b1d.kernel_post>;
  <verbatim|kernelPrices.margins>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Ground.lean>>|<cell|The
  parent\<#2019\>s <verbatim|sec:actual-global-row-prices> records the
  selected-history application of the actual Gram, panel covariance,
  panelization, inverse, and gap prices. No diagonal or posed-reader
  substitution is made.>>|<row|<cell|Source-row and move-row
  estimates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.MarginalMultiplier3b1d.SourceBounds.source_bound>,
  <verbatim|.move_bound>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Source.lean>>|<cell|These
  bound the actual source on frozen data and the actual move map on active
  coordinates. The manuscript uses the resulting all-period componentwise
  bound and rectangular row/column price in the finite matrix
  estimate.>>|<row|<cell|Auxiliary-row defect and broad-span
  implication>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.MarginalMultiplier3b1d.signal_bound>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.SectorChange.broad_span>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Force.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/SectorNext/GAUSSIAN_SECTOR_CHANGE/*>>|<cell|The defect is
  <verbatim|N-Q\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>>; the sign in the auxiliary-row
  identity is fixed by <verbatim|eta = -g\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>(Qm+b)>.
  With <verbatim|m=-N\<#1D40\>b>, this is
  <verbatim|-g\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>Q(Q\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>-N\<#1D40\>)b>.
  The coupling inverse bound follows from the selected beta
  band.>>|<row|<cell|All-matched response
  receipt>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Barge.Sound>,
  <verbatim|.dredge>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.Coffer.noises>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Dredge.lean>,
  <verbatim|Coffer.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|dredge> constructs one uniform
  <verbatim|Sound> estimate with quantifiers over stores, forests, tags and
  configurations. Its <verbatim|taxes> field is the endpoint Pours bound; its
  response fields are uniform over every pilot, not just a generic or dense
  subfamily.>>|<row|<cell|Exact endpoint palette and Pupil
  clauses>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.Grid.Pupil>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.ballot>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Acreage.lean>,
  <verbatim|Mezzanine.lean>>|<cell|The endpoint palette is exactly the
  clouded panel Gram matrix (<verbatim|Q_endpoint>). <verbatim|ballot> sets
  the nonnegative fee to <verbatim|\<varepsilon\>*fiery/coupling(beta)>, gets
  the credit clause from <verbatim|Sound.taxes>, and gets the socket clause
  from <verbatim|putAway> using the local certificates
  below.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform selected chart/beacon/annulus
  package>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.Granite>,
  <verbatim|.excels>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk.Beacons>,
  <verbatim|.Prognosis>, <verbatim|.torch>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Mezzanine.lean>,
  <verbatim|Wiggle.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|excels> chooses one width and
  beacon parameter and returns chart, annulus, deep-door and beacon receipts.
  <verbatim|torch> gets the CAB plateau key from
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticNext.ConnectedActivity.Jewels.night>, the CAB chart
  bound from <verbatim|.guard_broad>, and the mean-switch proposition from
  <verbatim|.prognosis>. The displayed subtraction identity is
  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticNext.ConnectedActivity.Aff.takes_sub>; its bounds are
  proved by <verbatim|.velocity> in <verbatim|Stint.lean>.
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk.peers> combines that
  coordinate estimate with <verbatim|.full_pose> and <verbatim|.same_face> to
  compare the actual portrait of the selected field with the CAB mean: two
  per-color errors <verbatim|x^(-7/8)> give <verbatim|2
  dim(G.ColorIndex)x^(-7/8)\<leq\>x^(-3/4)>. <verbatim|Wiggle.shelter> then
  identifies the CAB-sewn configuration with the actual physical field, by
  separate trunk, active and frozen-link cases. No CAB matrix/law is
  identified with actual reader matrices <verbatim|Q,C,N>.>>|<row|<cell|Outposts,
  port-to-log bridge, and far-door bound>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk.blaze>,
  <verbatim|.distant_links>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.DeepDoors>,
  <verbatim|.putAway>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/{Shield,Toe}.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|blaze>
  turns the local beacon receipts on the radius-<verbatim|B> neighborhood
  into faces, braid and frame outpost data. The port estimate sums the fixed
  macrobox face tolls and adds the connector chord; the logarithm chart and
  injectivity-ball identity then identify the actual tape.
  <verbatim|distant_links> applies this to obtain the uniform door-tape
  bound. <verbatim|putAway> uses the same store, forest, tag and field to
  show each of the five mask coordinates equals one.>>|<row|<cell|Toe
  separation and local gauge/chart estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk.full_pose>,
  <verbatim|.shelter>; seed-tree port estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Pairing.lean>,
  <verbatim|Wiggle.lean>, <verbatim|Toe.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|full_pose>
  constructs a based gauge chart at the toe. On the nonzero-socket branch the
  support foot is disjoint from the radius-300B store dome and contains the
  toe; nested domes imply the toe is outside radius 50B. The local beacon
  then applies at every site within B. The port estimate sums the fixed
  macrobox face costs and connector chord, and the logarithm chart identifies
  the tape. The elementary separation is source footfall(toe in foot) plus
  inclusion of radius-50B dome in radius-300B dome; no external geometry-port
  lemma is invoked. <verbatim|shelter> checks the actual same field on
  trunks, active coordinates and frozen coordinates.>>|<row|<cell|Public
  selected-history caller>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>;
  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.solaris>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Fares.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/*>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/*>>|<cell|The
  public selector chooses the selected history once. Its stored
  <verbatim|Nest>, <verbatim|Climbs>, <verbatim|Freight> and <verbatim|Makes>
  are passed to the same universal fare certificate at the actual
  <verbatim|Bolt> family; the palette estimates are uniform over every
  matched pilot in that stored family. <verbatim|solaris> supplies the
  eventual invitation conditions for each fixed section/grade, uniformly in
  period, rather than one cutoff common to all grades.>>>>>

  <section|Mathematical content and retained
  inputs><label|mathematical-content-and-retained-inputs>

  The weighted-response proposition proves its finite-dimensional
  inequalities from the rectangular row/column price. The (M^{\\mathsf T})
  orientation is essential: the source map takes active coordinates to
  response rows. The auxiliary estimate uses the inverse-defect price and the
  coupling inverse; the broad-span implication then turns a nonzero door into
  the (x^2) noise bound. The screened covariance\<#2019\>s common Pours cap
  is inherited from the uniform global-price unit.

  The local socket argument is on the same matched pilot throughout. A
  nonzero socket implies the branch where its support foot is disjoint from
  the store dome; the converse is not asserted. Toe separation, the beacon on
  every nearby site, the port sum, the logarithm chart and the far-door
  estimate then imply that each mask factor is one. The all-pilot quantifier
  is inherited from <verbatim|excels> and the uniform <verbatim|Sound>
  estimate; it is not obtained by a continuity or genericity argument.

  For the expanded CAB-to-actual beacon calculation, the rates are
  rho_(r,k)(x)=radiusB(x)^k fiery(x)^r; the key bought scales are rho_(2,25),
  rho_(2,26), rho_(2,27)\<leqslant\>x^(-7/8), rho_(2,29), and rho_(2,40). The
  final beacon fee is half the CAB plateau threshold. The local target
  payment uses delta=a_*/64 and the row-price choice epsilon_0=min(1,delta
  sqrt(omega_CAB)/(4(1+sqrt(dim(G_color)))W_row)); it bounds the shifted
  action by 2 W_row epsilon_0 t and splits the target into two delta t/2
  terms. The finite subtraction identity is
  YM.AnalyticNext.ConnectedActivity.Aff.takes_sub, its two paid terms are
  bounded by velocity in Stint.lean, the actual portrait comparison is peers
  using full_pose and same_face in Milk/Pairing.lean, the shift budget is
  prognosis, and the same-field identity is
  YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Milk.shelter in Wiggle.lean. The remaining
  plateau and broad-chart estimates are the precise reserve/wedge
  consequences of YM.AnalyticNext.ConnectedActivity.Jewels.night and
  guard_broad; their hypotheses are retained as the purchased uniform
  reserve, branch, wedge, and finite-chart data rather than confused with the
  actual matrix prices. The parent unit sec:actual-global-row-prices has
  passed independent review and supplies these selected-history bounds. No
  external literature result was used for the finite matrix arithmetic or the
  exact source-specific assembly.

